.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt PING 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ping
.Nd send ICMP echo requests
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar host
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
attempts four ping operations to
.Ar host ;
each may send up to four echo requests.
The default host is
.Ql 10.0.2.2 ,
QEMU's gateway.
Root privilege is not required.
.Pp
The host may be an IPv4 address or a name.
Names are looked up in
.Pa /etc/hosts ,
or
.Pa /hosts
when that file is absent, then through a DNS A query to the first valid
.Ql nameserver
in
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf ,
or
.Pa /resolv.conf
when that file is absent.
The default DNS server is
.Ql 10.0.2.3 .
The resolver retries for about six seconds unless a matching response
arrives.
.Pp
Each request uses the kernel's private
.Dv SC_PING
socket operation, described in
.Xr ping 2 .
The program issues a direct
.Xr socketcall 2
because musl has no wrapper for this operation.
It prints each reply's round-trip time in milliseconds, measured in
ticks of 10 ms, or reports a timeout.
.Pp
The kernel permits only one request in flight for the whole machine.
If another request is in flight, the operation fails with
.Er EBUSY
and
.Nm
exits with a busy-request diagnostic rather than reporting a timeout.
.Pp
On os-real, this program is installed as
.Pa /bin/ping .
BusyBox's ping applet is not built.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/resolv.conf
.It Pa /etc/hosts
Host names and addresses.
.It Pa /etc/resolv.conf
DNS server configuration.
.It Pa /hosts , /resolv.conf
The files read when the two above are absent.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
returns 0 if at least one reply arrives and no request fails with
.Er EBUSY .
It returns 1 if no replies arrive, the host cannot be resolved, or
another request is in flight.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl ping 10.0.2.2
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql ping: another ping in flight
Another ICMP echo request is in progress.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr busybox-networking 1 ,
.Xr nc 1 ,
.Xr ping 2
